A library system publishes overdue notifications to many independent patron dashboard widgets. The system keeps a list of registered listeners and calls them in a loop:

```java
public void publish(OverdueInfo info) {
    for (OverdueListener listener : listeners) {
        listener.onOverdue(info);
    }
}
```

Which statements about this design are correct?

A library's configuration class for return policies is written like this and is read from every request handler:

```java
public class ReturnConfig {
    private static ReturnConfig instance;
    private ReturnConfig() { }
    public static ReturnConfig getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new ReturnConfig();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```

Which criticisms of this code are justified?

A return processing workflow fixes the order of the steps and lets subclasses vary two of them:

```java
public abstract class ReturnWorkflow {
    public final Receipt process() {
        Data data = load();
        Data shaped = transform(data);
        return write(render(shaped));
    }
    protected Data load() { return Data.fromDefaultSource(); }
    protected abstract Data transform(Data data);
    protected abstract String render(Data data);
}
```

Which statements about this design are correct?

A library's return system sorts returned items with interchangeable algorithms:

```java
public interface ReturnSortStrategy { void performSort(List<Return> input); }
public class DateSort implements ReturnSortStrategy { ... }
public class PrioritySort implements ReturnSortStrategy { ... }
public class Context { private List<Return> returns; private ReturnSortStrategy sortAlgorithm; ... }
public class Policy { private Context context; public void configure() { ... } }
```

Using the class names from this listing: the class that holds the returns and a reference to the currently selected algorithm is [-spot 1]. The type that both `DateSort` and `PrioritySort` implement is [-spot 2]. The class whose `configure()` method decides which algorithm to select is [-spot 3].

